From 4e57901b0afbd3265e73cf2140dcc70665d6fa17 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] amigaos: -fuse-cxa-atexit by default (thread_local
 destructors run)

default_use_cxa_atexit=yes for m68k*-*-amigaos*, so cc1plus starts with
flag_use_cxa_atexit set (DEFAULT_USE_CXA_ATEXIT).

With -fno-use-cxa-atexit GCC never registers the destructor of a
thread_local at namespace scope or a static data member: handle_tls_init()
registers destructors only when flag_use_cxa_atexit is set, and there is
no destruction pass for thread-local storage. A plain m68k-amigaos-g++
build ran none of them, in a thread or in the main program. (A
thread_local inside a function was registered either way.)

With it, a static object's destructor is registered with
__cxa_atexit(dtor, obj, &__dso_handle) when the object is constructed,
and a thread_local's with libstdc++'s __cxa_thread_atexit(). Static
destructors then run in the reverse order of construction, interleaved
with atexit() functions, as C++ requires; before, they ran from
__DTOR_LIST__ after every atexit() function.

libnix provides __cxa_atexit and __dso_handle (gfopengcc
patches/libnix/0005); this patch needs it. -fno-use-cxa-atexit turns
the old way back on.
---
 gcc/config.gcc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config.gcc b/gcc/config.gcc
index 51b9ee119..6cf034acd 100644
--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ -2508,6 +2508,11 @@ m68k*-*-amigaos*)
 	extra_options="${extra_options} m68k/amigaos.opt"
 	extra_gcc_objs="driver-amigaos.o"
 	gnu_ld=yes
+	# GFOpenAmigaGCC: -fuse-cxa-atexit by default. GCC then registers every
+	# static and thread_local destructor (__cxa_atexit, __cxa_thread_atexit);
+	# without it a thread_local's destructor never runs. libnix provides
+	# __cxa_atexit and __dso_handle (gfopengcc patches/libnix/0005).
+	default_use_cxa_atexit=yes
 	CFLAGS="-Os"
   	case ${enable_threads} in
 	    yes | posix) thread_file='posix' ;;
-- 
2.53.0

